  {
    "paperId": "d9fefd47fe043befbc099cd2871161df5c52fcc6",
    "title": "ON CURVES OVER FINITE FIELDS WITH JACOBIANS OF SMALL EXPONENT",
    "year": 2006,
    "citationCount": 6,
    "authors": [
      "Kevin Ford",
      "I. Shparlinski"
    ],
    "venue": "",
    "abstract": "We show that finite fields over which there is a curve of a given genus g \u2265 1 with its Jacobian having a small exponent, are very rare. This extends a recent result of Duke in the case of g = 1. We also show that when g = 1 or g = 2, our lower bounds on the exponent, valid for almost all finite fields \ud835\udd3dq and all curves over \ud835\udd3dq, are best possible.",
